# upload change-detection flags written by uploadAll.sh
*/.upload-changed

# converter-source stamps: which code built the tree that is on this machine.
# Not committed, because they describe a local built tree -- a checkout whose
# stamp disagreed with its own hubs/ would either skip a rebuild it needs or
# force one it does not. The ucsc equivalents live under UCSC_BUILT_DIR and are
# outside the repo already.
*/.pipeline_hash
*/.derivation_hash

# pending-deploy marker written by run.sh
/.deploy-pending

# checkTrackUrls.mjs's rotation state: when each track url last answered, so a
# budgeted run knows which few thousand it still owes a probe. Local to whoever
# ran it, and committing it would churn the tree on every pass. CI keeps its own
# copy in the actions cache -- a miss there costs a restarted rotation, nothing
# more.
ucsc2jbrowse/.trackUrlCheck.json

# addGeneticCodes.ts's taxId -> mitochondrial genetic code answers from NCBI
# taxonomy. Derived, machine-local, and re-derivable in one round of efetch, so
# it is ignored for the same reasons as the rotation state above. It exists
# because this step has no needs_rebuild-style gate of its own: a broad
# PIPELINE_SOURCES marks all ~240 assemblies changed on any hubtools edit, and
# without the cache each of those runs re-queried NCBI and re-fetched a
# chrom.sizes per assembly from hgdownload.
ucsc2jbrowse/.mitoCodes.json

# vendored bed2gff Rust build output (source is committed, binary is not)
/bed2gff/target/

# astro sync artifacts at the repo root (website/ has its own rule)
.astro/
